  "notes": "General Biology option, University Park, standard MATH 140 start (the bulletin also has an ALEKS/MATH-21-remedial-start variant and a MATH-22/26-start variant). Uses the CHEM 210/212/213W organic-chemistry path rather than the CHEM 202/203 alternative, matching the University Park suggested plan. The '18 credits of 400-level biology, with at least 3 from each of 6 named groups (Plant and Fungi, Evolution, Genetics and Developmental Biology, Ecology, Physiology, Practicum)' requirement is modeled as 6 slots of 3 credits each (one per group) — the bulletin's own suggested plan does the same thing, listing these generically as 'BIOL 4XX' rather than specific codes, since each group has 20-30 alternative courses. 'Supporting Courses and Related Areas' (24-31 credits department-list electives) and remaining Gen Ed requirements are modeled as generic slots. 'etm' marks the courses everything else in the sequence assumes are done. Post-prereq-parser-fix repair, same as BIOL-2026.json: CHEM 110's real prereq is MATH 22, which was never in this plan -- and MATH 22 itself real-chains through MATH 21, MATH 4, and MATH 3, none of which were present either, leaving CHEM 110 (and everything after it: CHEM 111/112/113/210/212/213W) permanently unschedulable. Added MATH 3/MATH 4 (Semester 1) and MATH 21/MATH 22 (Semester 2) explicitly to complete the real chain. Bumped max_credits_per_semester from 17 to 18 to keep 4-year graduation achievable rather than dropping a real requirement.",
